WEBVTT

00:00:01.350 --> 00:00:05.980
In the Xyz Dimension, Academia turned 
Heartland City's

00:00:05.980 --> 00:00:09.690
defenseless citizens into cards, one by one.

00:00:10.160 --> 00:00:12.060
Duels aren't tools of war!

00:00:12.920 --> 00:00:16.960
A true duel brings smiles to everyone!

00:00:20.930 --> 00:00:22.460
Wow.

00:00:22.460 --> 00:00:25.100
I've never seen a duel like that before!

00:00:25.750 --> 00:00:28.680
This is a real duel...

00:00:29.340 --> 00:00:30.540
Damn!

00:00:38.160 --> 00:00:40.120
There are still others?

00:00:42.760 --> 00:00:45.590
Are you ready to make your confession?

00:00:50.460 --> 00:00:52.330
The Aquaria Project.

00:00:53.110 --> 00:00:58.100
In their plan to create an ideal world, 
the Fusion Dimension's Academia

00:00:58.520 --> 00:01:03.480
has driven Heartland City, in the Xyz 
Dimension, to the brink of obliteration.

00:02:37.200 --> 00:02:42.010
Eyes of Galaxy

00:02:45.260 --> 00:02:47.180
Why would you do this?

00:02:47.180 --> 00:02:47.980
Why?

00:02:47.980 --> 00:02:51.000
Why else? They're Academia.

00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:52.450
My enemies!

00:02:52.800 --> 00:02:56.170
You can't turn people into cards just 
because they're your enemies.

00:02:56.170 --> 00:02:59.040
That makes you no different from Academia!

00:02:59.040 --> 00:03:00.160
That's right...

00:03:00.160 --> 00:03:03.640
You don't mind using the most 
despicable methods?!

00:03:03.640 --> 00:03:07.070
Not long ago, you tried to do the same thing.

00:03:07.870 --> 00:03:09.730
Are you with the Resistance?

00:03:10.030 --> 00:03:13.500
I'd heard the Resistance was 
destroyed. Glad to see you.

00:03:13.500 --> 00:03:18.340
You're glad? Because it means 
more prey to hunt?

00:03:18.340 --> 00:03:20.410
No! We're on your side!

00:03:20.410 --> 00:03:22.360
I will determine that.

00:03:22.360 --> 00:03:23.340
Determine?

00:03:25.550 --> 00:03:30.090
They've used various methods to
 toy with us during their "hunt."

00:03:30.090 --> 00:03:31.990
So I made up my mind.

00:03:31.990 --> 00:03:35.240
I would use my duel to determine 
who is friend or foe.

00:03:35.240 --> 00:03:36.530
Now, prepare yourselves!

00:03:36.530 --> 00:03:39.500
Sounds fun... Let's do it.

00:03:39.770 --> 00:03:40.700
Sawatari!

00:03:40.970 --> 00:03:43.040
Don't rise to his provocation.

00:03:43.040 --> 00:03:47.200
Shut up! After I let those guys go, 
he turned them into cards.

00:03:47.200 --> 00:03:49.550
And he'll decide if we're friends or foes?

00:03:49.550 --> 00:03:52.990
I can't stand by and listen to such 
self-centered nonsense.

00:03:52.990 --> 00:03:55.500
It's clear enough to me...

00:03:56.050 --> 00:03:57.520
You are our enemy!

00:03:57.990 --> 00:04:00.220
I'm nice, so I won't turn you into a card,

00:04:00.220 --> 00:04:02.950
but I'm going to set you straight!

00:04:03.400 --> 00:04:04.570
Prepare yourself!

00:04:06.520 --> 00:04:08.830
Action Field, on.

00:04:09.440 --> 00:04:11.820
Field Spell Crossover.

00:04:15.270 --> 00:04:16.950
Action Field?

00:04:19.680 --> 00:04:21.960
That's right... This is how I duel.

00:04:21.960 --> 00:04:25.240
Hey! It isn't just your method!

00:04:25.240 --> 00:04:27.680
Action Duels are the Lancers'—

00:04:27.680 --> 00:04:29.610
Don't nitpick.

00:04:29.610 --> 00:04:31.690
Anyway, time for my long-awaited return.

00:04:31.690 --> 00:04:33.380
Get in the mood, apprentices!

00:04:33.380 --> 00:04:34.830
Apprentices?

00:04:34.830 --> 00:04:36.090
Outrageous!

00:04:36.480 --> 00:04:39.290
The duelists meet at the battlefield!

00:04:39.290 --> 00:04:42.490
A-Along with their monsters, 
they'll kick the ground...

00:04:42.860 --> 00:04:44.700
...to move around the field.

00:04:44.970 --> 00:04:48.170
Witness dueling's greatest evolution!

00:04:48.510 --> 00:04:49.730
Action...

00:04:50.040 --> 00:04:50.970
Duel!

00:04:51.700 --> 00:04:53.480
I take the first turn.

00:04:53.480 --> 00:04:56.910
I summon Abyss Actor — Wild Hope!

00:05:00.380 --> 00:05:03.850
Then, I set one card and end my turn.

00:05:03.850 --> 00:05:05.660
Action Duel?

00:05:05.660 --> 00:05:06.820
Wait!

00:05:06.820 --> 00:05:10.560
I, the man Gongenzaka, 
will participate in this duel!

00:05:10.560 --> 00:05:13.400
2000-point penalty for entering the battle.

00:05:15.560 --> 00:05:17.200
Gongenzaka! You, too?

00:05:17.200 --> 00:05:19.860
My turn... Draw!

00:05:21.070 --> 00:05:25.040
I summon Superheavy Samurai 
Swordsman from my hand!

00:05:28.240 --> 00:05:32.320
Usually, you focus on defense first,

00:05:32.320 --> 00:05:34.980
but you summoned in attack position?

00:05:35.260 --> 00:05:39.150
That arrogant fool must have 
really made you mad.

00:05:39.150 --> 00:05:40.850
Okay, go ahead!

00:05:40.850 --> 00:05:42.820
Hit him with everything you have!

00:05:43.100 --> 00:05:45.160
No, I will not move!

00:05:46.110 --> 00:05:48.820
And neither will you. Or he.

00:05:49.880 --> 00:05:54.070
I activate the effect of Superheavy Samurai 
Soulpeacemaker in my hand,

00:05:54.070 --> 00:05:56.750
and equip it to Swordsman!

00:05:56.750 --> 00:06:01.510
From now on, no one can attack 
anything but Swordsman!

00:06:01.510 --> 00:06:02.470
And...

00:06:03.020 --> 00:06:04.780
Swordsman has the ability

00:06:04.780 --> 00:06:08.710
to reduce the attack points 
of the monster it fights to 0.

00:06:09.040 --> 00:06:11.420
With 0 attack points, you can't win a fight.

00:06:11.840 --> 00:06:14.120
Thus, no one can attack.

00:06:14.690 --> 00:06:16.080
Yes.

00:06:16.080 --> 00:06:19.100
Yelling at them to stop will 
accomplish nothing.

00:06:19.100 --> 00:06:23.270
But I cannot allow that man and Sawatari 
to attack each other directly.

00:06:24.020 --> 00:06:26.940
I don't know if he's Resistance or not,

00:06:26.940 --> 00:06:29.700
but right now, we need all 
the allies we can get.

00:06:29.700 --> 00:06:33.910
This is no time for Academia's enemies 
to be fighting each other!

00:06:34.420 --> 00:06:35.960
Great job, Gongenzaka.

00:06:35.960 --> 00:06:38.800
Now no one can move or hurt each other!

00:06:38.800 --> 00:06:40.610
This is the true immovable duel!

00:06:40.610 --> 00:06:42.240
Immovable?

00:06:42.240 --> 00:06:44.950
If you don't want to move, I'll go on my own!

00:06:48.640 --> 00:06:52.230
I activate my Action Spell Broken Ruin!

00:06:52.230 --> 00:06:57.240
This card deals damage that's 300 
times the difference between

00:06:57.240 --> 00:06:59.530
the number of cards in my hand and yours.

00:06:59.900 --> 00:07:02.190
I have three cards, and you have five.

00:07:02.190 --> 00:07:04.740
That's a difference of 2, for 600 total damage!

00:07:10.680 --> 00:07:16.110
When effect damage is dealt, Superheavy 
Samurai Swordsman is destroyed.

00:07:17.670 --> 00:07:20.300
You see? This is how an Action Duel works!

00:07:20.300 --> 00:07:23.320
Immovable duels are no good for anyone.

00:07:23.610 --> 00:07:25.820
You little rat...

00:07:25.820 --> 00:07:28.790
I thought you and Yuya had 
reached an understanding.

00:07:29.700 --> 00:07:31.000
Understanding?

00:07:31.000 --> 00:07:33.440
Consider our position!

00:07:33.440 --> 00:07:35.500
Academia controls this place.

00:07:35.500 --> 00:07:37.700
What good comes of allies 
fighting each other?

00:07:37.700 --> 00:07:41.040
I never said I was your ally.

00:07:41.800 --> 00:07:45.740
I said I'd let my duel determine 
if you were friend or foe.

00:07:45.740 --> 00:07:48.190
But I have my conclusion now.

00:07:48.190 --> 00:07:50.990
Action Fields... Action Spells.

00:07:50.990 --> 00:07:55.990
No one in the Heartland City, where I 
was born and raised, duels like that.

00:07:56.580 --> 00:07:59.630
In other words, you're invaders 
from another dimension,

00:07:59.630 --> 00:08:01.190
Heartland's enemies!

00:08:01.730 --> 00:08:05.340
When you said you wouldn't move, 
that was the end of your turn.

00:08:05.340 --> 00:08:06.560
That means it's...

00:08:06.900 --> 00:08:08.030
My turn!

00:08:09.270 --> 00:08:12.740
I summon Cipher Wing from my hand!

00:08:15.570 --> 00:08:16.940
Cipher...

00:08:17.450 --> 00:08:20.140
When there's a Cipher Wing 
on my side of the field,

00:08:20.410 --> 00:08:23.920
I can Special Summon another 
Cipher Wing from my hand.

00:08:23.920 --> 00:08:27.450
Two Level 4s. This is the Xyz Dimension.

00:08:28.040 --> 00:08:30.390
Having two monsters of one level means...

00:08:30.390 --> 00:08:32.090
I won't let you!

00:08:32.090 --> 00:08:35.290
I activate my Continuous Trap 
Abyss Actor's Injury!

00:08:35.760 --> 00:08:38.200
I choose one monster on the field.

00:08:38.200 --> 00:08:40.800
And monsters of the same level

00:08:40.800 --> 00:08:43.500
can't be used as components 
in a Special Summon.

00:08:43.950 --> 00:08:46.970
I choose Level 4 Cipher Wing!

00:08:49.470 --> 00:08:53.210
Now, you can't perform a Level 4 Xyz Summon.

00:08:53.210 --> 00:08:57.150
Did you set that trap because 
you knew from the start...

00:08:57.440 --> 00:08:58.890
Of course.

00:08:58.890 --> 00:09:03.020
When we came here, he had that 
dragon I'd never seen before.

00:09:04.700 --> 00:09:07.190
That must be his ace monster.

00:09:07.990 --> 00:09:13.500
In this Academia-occupied town, 
he's been fighting and surviving.

00:09:13.500 --> 00:09:16.970
Which means he must be quite 
skilled, with strong monsters.

00:09:16.970 --> 00:09:18.670
To beat a guy like that...

00:09:18.970 --> 00:09:23.370
Keeping his ace monster sealed 
is the best strategy, eh?

00:09:23.370 --> 00:09:25.450
It seems you understand.

00:09:25.450 --> 00:09:28.660
Well, have we finally come 
to an understanding, too?

00:09:29.540 --> 00:09:31.500
I do see what you're after.

00:09:31.500 --> 00:09:34.060
But you understand nothing!

00:09:35.160 --> 00:09:38.690
I'm telling you to stop this fight right now.

00:09:38.990 --> 00:09:41.160
Even if you win now, the next—

00:09:41.160 --> 00:09:42.360
No, you can't win.

00:09:44.120 --> 00:09:46.560
If you think this is enough to beat Kaito—

00:09:47.120 --> 00:09:48.370
Kaito?

00:09:48.370 --> 00:09:50.420
Is that his name?

00:09:50.420 --> 00:09:51.850
Why do I know that?

00:09:52.550 --> 00:09:55.190
Ute... Is it Ute?

00:09:55.700 --> 00:09:58.530
Are you telling me about him?

00:09:58.530 --> 00:10:00.910
Yes, he is Kaito.

00:10:00.910 --> 00:10:03.550
In Heartland, he is a famous duelist.

00:10:04.150 --> 00:10:07.290
He looks different from how he used to.

00:10:09.080 --> 00:10:11.720
But that monster is definitely...

00:10:11.720 --> 00:10:15.690
I activate my Continuous Spell Cipher 
Interference from my hand!

00:10:17.720 --> 00:10:21.870
When there are two or more of the 
same Cipher monster on my field,

00:10:22.120 --> 00:10:26.860
I can double the attack points 
of one, during battle.

00:10:29.040 --> 00:10:30.210
Battle!

00:10:30.210 --> 00:10:33.710
I attack Abyss Actor — Wild Hope
 with Cipher Wing!

00:10:36.150 --> 00:10:39.320
In that instant, Wild Hope's effect activates!

00:10:39.320 --> 00:10:41.240
When this card is destroyed,

00:10:41.240 --> 00:10:44.890
I can add one Abyss Actor monster 
from my deck to my hand.

00:10:45.230 --> 00:10:48.360
I attack directly with my other Cipher Wing!

00:10:53.100 --> 00:10:54.300
Sawatari!

00:10:54.640 --> 00:10:58.500
In that instant, the effect of 
Cipher Interference ends.

00:11:01.630 --> 00:11:04.440
I set two cards and end my turn.

00:11:06.180 --> 00:11:08.160
Get a grip, Sawatari.

00:11:08.160 --> 00:11:10.380
The duel is only getting started!

00:11:10.880 --> 00:11:12.380
Kaito was strong.

00:11:13.190 --> 00:11:15.340
Before Academia's invasion,

00:11:15.340 --> 00:11:19.210
it was believed he would become 
Heartland's new duel champion.

00:11:19.620 --> 00:11:21.310
Duel champion?

00:11:21.310 --> 00:11:25.950
But at that time, Kaito's duels had warmth.

00:11:26.370 --> 00:11:30.740
Now, anger is all that's there.

00:11:31.210 --> 00:11:32.440
Anger?

00:11:32.440 --> 00:11:33.350
Yes.

00:11:34.690 --> 00:11:38.070
Since I've been gone, 
what's happened to him?

00:11:41.320 --> 00:11:43.580
I'm mad now!

00:11:43.580 --> 00:11:45.560
In this Academia-occupied city,

00:11:45.560 --> 00:11:49.200
you were fighting alone, so I 
was thinking of going easy...

00:11:49.200 --> 00:11:51.320
But now, I'm serious.

00:11:51.320 --> 00:11:52.880
My turn!

00:11:52.880 --> 00:11:54.090
In that case,

00:11:54.090 --> 00:11:57.520
I set the Pendulum Scale with 
Scale 1 Abyss Actor — Evil Heel

00:11:57.520 --> 00:12:02.810
and Scale 8 Abyss Actor — Funky Comedian.

00:12:12.480 --> 00:12:16.680
Now I can summon monsters between 
Levels 2 and 7 simultaneously.

00:12:16.970 --> 00:12:17.880
Simultaneously?

00:12:17.880 --> 00:12:19.470
Pendulum Summon!

00:12:19.470 --> 00:12:21.890
Come out, my monsters!

00:12:22.670 --> 00:12:25.630
First, from my hand, 
Abyss Actor — Superstar!

00:12:25.630 --> 00:12:30.090
Then, return from my Extra Deck, 
Abyss Actor — Wild Hope!

00:12:30.090 --> 00:12:33.560
Destroyed monsters, returning from 
his Extra Deck?

00:12:33.560 --> 00:12:35.420
Pendulum Summon...

00:12:36.320 --> 00:12:41.240
Back then, Syun and I were studying at the 
Spade Branch of Heartland's duel school.

00:12:41.750 --> 00:12:44.910
Kaito was the ace of our rival, Clover Branch.

00:12:45.520 --> 00:12:48.120
His style was subtle but bold.

00:12:48.120 --> 00:12:53.020
His instinctive read of opponents' tactics 
outstripped that of anyone else.

00:12:53.320 --> 00:12:55.220
Superstar's monster effect!

00:12:56.020 --> 00:12:57.600
Once per turn,

00:12:57.600 --> 00:13:02.660
I can add one Abyss Script spell 
from my deck to my hand!

00:13:03.250 --> 00:13:09.870
And I equip the spell card I added, 
Fire Dragon's Lair, to Superstar!

00:13:10.660 --> 00:13:14.070
Now, when Superstar destroys 
one of your monsters,

00:13:14.070 --> 00:13:18.080
I can banish three cards from your Extra Deck.

00:13:18.790 --> 00:13:23.050
Of course! He means to banish the 
dragons in Kaito's extra deck!

00:13:23.050 --> 00:13:27.770
Then, I activate Continuous Spell 
Abyss Actors' Costume Chest!

00:13:27.770 --> 00:13:31.320
Once per turn, I can activate one 
Abyss Costume from my deck.

00:13:31.320 --> 00:13:35.530
I choose Abyss Costume — Hero's 
Sword, and equip it to Superstar!

00:13:40.800 --> 00:13:44.140
This causes Superstar's attack 
points to increase by 300.

00:13:44.390 --> 00:13:47.640
Next, Funky Comedian's Pendulum Effect!

00:13:47.640 --> 00:13:49.370
Pendulum Effect?

00:13:49.370 --> 00:13:50.950
Once per turn,

00:13:50.950 --> 00:13:56.430
I can add one Abyss Actor Pendulum Monster,
 faceup, to my Extra Deck.

00:13:56.430 --> 00:14:00.480
And that monster's attack points can be 
added to those of another monster

00:14:00.480 --> 00:14:02.690
until my End Phase!

00:14:02.690 --> 00:14:05.390
I add Wild Hope to my Extra Deck.

00:14:05.390 --> 00:14:10.680
Superstar's attack points increase 
by 1600, those of Wild Hope!

00:14:11.360 --> 00:14:14.830
Battle, Superstar! Attack Cipher Wing!

00:14:15.160 --> 00:14:18.070
I'm going to banish your dragon!

00:14:18.070 --> 00:14:22.270
In that instant, Continuous Spell 
Cipher Interference's effect

00:14:22.270 --> 00:14:25.590
doubles Cipher Wing's attack points!

00:14:26.420 --> 00:14:30.110
And I activate my Continuous 
Trap Cipher Shield!

00:14:31.900 --> 00:14:35.520
When there are two or more Cipher 
monsters on my side of the field,

00:14:35.520 --> 00:14:38.420
Cipher monsters cannot be 
destroyed by battle!

00:14:41.130 --> 00:14:46.230
Damn... I dealt damage, but I 
couldn't banish the dragons.

00:14:46.560 --> 00:14:50.350
In that instant, Continuous Trap 
Cipher Chain activates!

00:14:50.350 --> 00:14:52.100
When I take battle damage,

00:14:52.100 --> 00:14:55.440
I can activate this, targeting all 
monsters on the field.

00:14:58.940 --> 00:14:59.910
What?

00:15:00.900 --> 00:15:04.870
If any monster linked by this effect

00:15:04.870 --> 00:15:07.390
is destroyed, all of them are.

00:15:07.390 --> 00:15:12.590
And the sum of their attack points is 
dealt to all players as damage!

00:15:12.590 --> 00:15:16.060
The sum of all their attack points?

00:15:16.060 --> 00:15:18.060
N-Not bad...

00:15:18.520 --> 00:15:22.700
You can summon as many monsters as 
you want with Pendulum Summon,

00:15:22.700 --> 00:15:24.540
but I'll destroy them all.

00:15:24.540 --> 00:15:27.870
However, you're the only ones 
who will take the damage.

00:15:28.350 --> 00:15:33.340
With Continuous Trap Cipher Shield 
activated, I don't take effect damage.

00:15:33.750 --> 00:15:38.320
At the end of the Battle Phase, 
Cipher Interference's effect ends.

00:15:38.320 --> 00:15:42.020
I-Is this how he, how Kaito, duels?

00:15:42.020 --> 00:15:42.980
No...

00:15:43.960 --> 00:15:45.900
He was certainly bold,

00:15:45.900 --> 00:15:50.230
but when I knew him, he'd never 
have dueled so mercilessly.

00:15:50.620 --> 00:15:52.650
I end my turn.

00:15:52.650 --> 00:15:56.430
In that instant, Funky Comedian's 
Pendulum Effect ends,

00:15:56.430 --> 00:15:59.050
and Superstar's attack points return to normal.

00:15:59.470 --> 00:16:03.570
At least I avoided 1600 damage.

00:16:03.570 --> 00:16:05.670
It's a drop in the bucket!

00:16:05.670 --> 00:16:09.100
The sum of their attack points is still 6600!

00:16:09.800 --> 00:16:13.280
No, there's only one way to turn this around.

00:16:14.490 --> 00:16:16.900
My turn!

00:16:18.590 --> 00:16:21.560
I summon Superheavy Samurai Flutist!

00:16:26.430 --> 00:16:30.270
And I send Superheavy Samurai Soulbeads 
from my hand to the graveyard,

00:16:30.600 --> 00:16:34.860
to Special Summon Tuner Monster 
Superheavy Samurai Trumpeter!

00:16:38.440 --> 00:16:44.650
Level 2 Trumpeter tunes Level 3 
Swordsman and Level 2 Flutist!

00:16:44.910 --> 00:16:47.240
Shinobi who hides in darkness,

00:16:47.240 --> 00:16:51.830
appear on this wasteland of a battlefield, 
with a roar that echoes over mountains.

00:16:52.890 --> 00:16:54.260
Synchro Summon!

00:16:54.760 --> 00:16:58.490
Take the field, Superheavy Samurai Ninja Sarutobi!

00:16:59.000 --> 00:17:00.970
I activate Sarutobi's effect!

00:17:03.230 --> 00:17:07.760
Once per turn, if I have no spells 
or traps in my graveyard,

00:17:07.760 --> 00:17:11.110
I can destroy one spell or trap 
card on your side of the field,

00:17:11.110 --> 00:17:13.580
dealing 500 damage to you.

00:17:13.580 --> 00:17:16.580
I destroy Cipher Chain!

00:17:20.520 --> 00:17:23.990
Cipher Shield prevents me from 
taking effect damage.

00:17:24.960 --> 00:17:28.690
I activate the effect of Abyss 
Actors' Costume Chest,

00:17:29.280 --> 00:17:33.440
to add Abyss Costume — 
Dwarf's Shield to my hand.

00:17:33.440 --> 00:17:36.220
I owe you, Gongenzaka...

00:17:36.220 --> 00:17:38.670
Here's my thank you. Take it!

00:17:40.700 --> 00:17:43.520
I equip Dwarf's Shield to Sarutobi.

00:17:43.520 --> 00:17:46.080
Its defense points increase by 300.

00:17:46.080 --> 00:17:49.550
Battle! I attack Cipher Wing with Sarutobi!

00:17:50.110 --> 00:17:54.700
Superheavy Samurai Ninja Sarutobi 
can attack from defense position!

00:17:57.950 --> 00:18:00.660
Continuous Spell Cipher Interference's effect

00:18:00.660 --> 00:18:03.360
doubles Cipher Wing's attack points!

00:18:03.630 --> 00:18:08.570
And Continuous Trap Cipher Shield's effect 
prevents Cipher Wing's destruction.

00:18:08.570 --> 00:18:10.270
But you still take the damage.

00:18:12.710 --> 00:18:15.740
In that instant, Cipher Interference's effect ends.

00:18:18.210 --> 00:18:20.440
I end my turn.

00:18:20.790 --> 00:18:24.950
Thanks to Gongenzaka, they don't have 
to worry about Cipher Chain.

00:18:24.950 --> 00:18:28.040
But his monsters are still strong.

00:18:28.040 --> 00:18:28.920
Yeah.

00:18:28.920 --> 00:18:33.050
As long as he has Xyz components, 
they can't rest easy.

00:18:33.050 --> 00:18:34.330
What are you talking about?

00:18:34.330 --> 00:18:36.330
Have you forgotten?

00:18:36.330 --> 00:18:39.640
The effect of my Continuous 
Trap Abyss Actor's Injury

00:18:39.640 --> 00:18:43.530
means he can't use Level 4 monsters 
as Special Summon components.

00:18:43.530 --> 00:18:45.580
Let me tell you once more!

00:18:45.580 --> 00:18:49.010
No matter how you struggle, 
you can't Xyz Summon!

00:18:49.010 --> 00:18:50.520
Are you sure about that?

00:18:50.520 --> 00:18:51.380
What?

00:18:52.540 --> 00:18:53.680
My turn.

00:18:53.680 --> 00:18:56.680
I summon a third Cipher Wing!

00:18:59.150 --> 00:19:02.300
But another Level 4 still won't let you Xyz—

00:19:02.300 --> 00:19:04.470
Who said it was Level 4?

00:19:05.110 --> 00:19:09.440
I tribute the third Cipher Wing 
to activate its monster effect!

00:19:10.350 --> 00:19:13.560
I raise the levels of all Cipher 
monsters on the field by 4.

00:19:16.770 --> 00:19:18.540
They're both Level 8!

00:19:18.960 --> 00:19:22.900
I overlay my two Level 8 Cipher Wings!

00:19:29.530 --> 00:19:31.590
Galaxy shining in the darkness...

00:19:31.890 --> 00:19:35.450
Dwell within the god of vengeance 
and become my servant!

00:19:38.090 --> 00:19:39.560
Xyz Summon!

00:19:39.980 --> 00:19:45.820
Descend, Rank 8 Galaxy-Eyes Cipher Dragon!

00:19:47.530 --> 00:19:50.460
Galaxy-Eyes Cipher Dragon...

00:19:50.460 --> 00:19:53.000
I sense tremendous rage in this monster.

00:19:53.400 --> 00:19:56.470
Like it's a vessel for Kaito's rage.

00:19:56.760 --> 00:19:59.520
There's nowhere left for you to run.

00:19:59.520 --> 00:20:02.450
Even if you beg for your lives, 
I won't listen to you.

00:20:02.750 --> 00:20:05.150
Rank 8 is scary,

00:20:05.150 --> 00:20:09.580
but when Pendulum Monsters are destroyed, 
they're sent to my Extra Deck.

00:20:09.580 --> 00:20:12.690
And on my next turn, I can Pendulum 
Summon them again.

00:20:12.690 --> 00:20:14.160
You won't get a next turn!

00:20:15.130 --> 00:20:21.690
I use one Overlay Unit to activate the effect 
of Galaxy-Eyes Cipher Dragon!

00:20:21.690 --> 00:20:23.640
Cipher Projection!

00:20:24.270 --> 00:20:29.660
Once per turn, until my End Phase, I can 
take control of one of your monsters,

00:20:29.660 --> 00:20:31.310
with its effect negated!

00:20:33.680 --> 00:20:34.880
Sarutobi!

00:20:35.240 --> 00:20:39.240
And Sarutobi is treated as a 
Galaxy-Eyes Cipher Dragon,

00:20:39.240 --> 00:20:41.320
with the same attack points.

00:20:41.320 --> 00:20:43.420
I switch Sarutobi to attack position!

00:20:45.820 --> 00:20:48.290
He has two dragons...

00:20:48.290 --> 00:20:49.260
Battle!

00:20:49.260 --> 00:20:53.130
I attack Abyss Actor — Superstar with 
the Galaxy-Eyes Cipher Dragon

00:20:53.130 --> 00:20:55.470
that Sarutobi became!

00:20:55.470 --> 00:20:58.830
When two Cipher monsters are on my field,

00:20:58.830 --> 00:21:01.740
Continuous Spell Cipher Interference's effect

00:21:01.740 --> 00:21:05.720
doubles the attack points of 
one monster in battle!

00:21:08.520 --> 00:21:10.810
Are you ready to make your confession?

00:21:11.780 --> 00:21:14.290
Annihilating Cipher Stream!

00:21:21.390 --> 00:21:23.200
You're finished, too!

00:21:23.200 --> 00:21:27.000
Galaxy-Eyes Cipher Dragon attacks directly!

00:21:33.070 --> 00:21:34.430
Gongenzaka...

00:21:34.430 --> 00:21:35.410
Sawatari!

00:21:35.410 --> 00:21:36.510
You won't escape, either!

00:21:38.220 --> 00:21:41.180
You'll become a card with the other two.

00:21:41.570 --> 00:21:45.120
I won't let anyone else be turned into a card!

00:21:45.400 --> 00:21:47.290
Not Sawatari. Not Gongenzaka.

00:21:47.290 --> 00:21:49.590
Not the Heartland survivors.

00:21:49.960 --> 00:21:51.600
Not the Academia soldiers!

00:21:51.600 --> 00:21:52.420
It's no use.

00:21:52.880 --> 00:21:55.790
Right now, Kaito's in no mood to listen.

00:21:55.790 --> 00:21:59.500
Whether or not he'll listen, 
I'll reach him with a duel.

00:21:59.970 --> 00:22:03.470
I learned in City, during my duel with Jack,

00:22:03.470 --> 00:22:07.440
that if I put my words, my thoughts, into a duel...

00:22:07.870 --> 00:22:10.090
Kaito and I can reach an understanding!

00:23:50.870 --> 00:23:54.540
If you know my name, then you 
must be from Academia.

00:23:54.540 --> 00:23:58.080
No! I just want to use this duel 
to communicate with you!

00:23:58.080 --> 00:23:59.180
It's no use, Yuya...

00:23:59.180 --> 00:24:02.320
As he is now, Kaito won't listen to you.

00:24:02.320 --> 00:24:06.390
But if I put my feelings into my duel, even Kaito...

00:24:06.390 --> 00:24:10.440
Words mean nothing! All that 
matters is burying Academia!

00:24:11.030 --> 00:24:14.810
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh! ARC-V: 
The Heartless Hunter.

00:24:14.810 --> 00:24:16.630
The fun is only getting started!
